{
  "id": "CHAIN-001",
  "name": "validation bypass → query primitive → privileged state transition",
  "description": "A three-file attack chain whose composition is the only reportable thing. A.py holds the discrepancy: handle_request coerces the filter, run_import does not. B.py holds the primitive: the report SQL is built by concatenation, and every caller that reaches it today passes integers, so it cannot be driven. C.py holds the privileged transition: it copies a role out of a report row onto the session, and while the query can only be driven with integers that role is the database's choice. None of the three is a finding alone; A→B→C crosses the boundary.\n\nThe replay submits only research deltas — the material an agent would have produced across rounds — and checks that the runtime keeps B alive while it is blocked, reopens it when A removes the blocker, and ends with a verified path from the objective's initial capability to its goal. Sources are real files in this directory, so a harness run has something to read; the evaluator copies them into the replay root so evidence references resolve to real line numbers.",
